    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d88-a4">

                <pb facs="0251" n="117" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg117"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 538.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Messrs. Sperry &amp; Co. to
                        Mr. Rice.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Francisco</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-12-05"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 5,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Regarding your inquiries concerning the
                    rebate in duties at the port of San Jose de Costa Rica, would say that our
                    customers in Costa Rica have advised us that we should ship by the
                    Spanish-American line, as they are able to collect 5 per cent, rebate on the
                    duties, and they have also inclosed us advertisements cut from their papers
                    stating such to be the case.</p>
                <p>Hoping this will be satisfactory, we are, etc.,</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sperry</hi> &amp; Co.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
